The outer boundary needs to be more complex:
Split the boundary edge that's facing the central area into SAW_TOOTH_COUNT_X * 2 or SAW_TOOTH_COUNT_Y * 2 parts with additional vertices.
Every odd vertex must be moved towards the central area by SAW_TOOTH_DEPTH.
Even vertices remain at the edge. This will give the outer boundary a saw-shaped inner surface which should help break down the larger triangles near the boundary.